{"uid":"808b787fd0c57f88","name":"test_check_hat_routes_never_consults_poisoned_ambient_home","fullName":"tests.test_llm_routes_requires_home#test_check_hat_routes_never_consults_poisoned_ambient_home","historyId":"cebe6466ad517fd39a51661dba1a261e","time":{"start":1791958317808,"stop":1791958317811,"duration":3},"description":"The ambient `$HOME` declares only `unrelated-provider` -- a\n    provider `cfg`'s own ref never names. The *explicit* `home` passed in\n    declares `good-provider`, which `cfg`'s ref DOES name. If\n    `check_hat_routes` ever fell back to (or merely consulted) the\n    ambient `$HOME`, it would see only `unrelated-provider` and raise\n    `UnroutableHatModel` naming it as the sole available provider. It must\n    not: the explicit `home` alone decides, so this must pass clean.","descriptionHtml":"<p>The ambient <code>$HOME</code> declares only <code>unrelated-provider</code> -- a<br />\nprovider <code>cfg</code>'s own ref never names. The <em>explicit</em> <code>home</code> passed in<br />\ndeclares <code>good-provider</code>, which <code>cfg</code>'s ref DOES name. If<br />\n<code>check_hat_routes</code> ever fell back to (or merely consulted) the<br />\nambient <code>$HOME</code>, it would see only <code>unrelated-provider</code> and raise<br />\n<code>UnroutableHatModel</code> naming it as the sole available provider. It must<br />\nnot: the explicit <code>home</code> alone decides, so this must pass clean.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791957838565,"stop":1791957838565,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791957838566,"stop":1791957838566,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"att